  t('<b>Also</b>', '<b>12 nautical miles:</b> Central administration, but States can tax activity there', '<b>Stamp duties</b> on legal agreements still State', w=14),
  sec('7 · BENEFITS, CHALLENGES, COMPENSATION, RNR ' + P('Mains GST, compensation'), 'g'),
  t('<b>Benefits</b>', 'simple, efficient; wider growing base = compliance (earlier honest paid evader’s share)', '<b>ITC across Centre and State taxes</b> = biggest reform; harmonised administration; automated <b>GSTN</b>', '<b>Compliance logic:</b> low cost of compliance, high cost of non-compliance; <b>system</b> catches evader, not an officer (earlier penalty = bribe)', t('<b>Handout page 13 (12 items)</b>', 'less cascading, lower prices, common national market, small taxpayers (EODB), self-regulating electronic system (fewer black transactions)', 'simplified regime, informed consumer, consumption-based tax and CST abolished (poorer States gain), exports zero-rated, IGST protects industry (Make in India)'), w=18),
  t('<b>Challenges</b>', '<b>Multiple slabs 0, 5, 12, 18, 28%</b> (2022); raw agri produce zero-rated; luxury and negative-externality goods <b>cess</b> above 28%; most important', 'filings (e.g. <b>GSTR-3B</b>) fell but still above earlier “zero”', '<b>Lobbying and politicisation:</b> food processing seeks zero rating; Centre’s Council majority accused of election-time cuts', '<b>One flat rate = regressive</b>; slabs add progressive element (0/5% necessities; 18% and 28% + cess luxury and demerit)', w=18),
  t('<b>Compensation to States</b>', 'pre-2017 revenue base; assumed <b>14%</b> nominal growth a year for <b>five years (till 2022)</b>', 'Centre pays shortfall, only <b>on account of GST implementation</b> (not State failure or pandemic)', '<b>GST compensation cess</b> on luxury and demerit goods; meant to end 2022; continuing “thanks to Covid”', w=18),
  t('<b>Revenue Neutral Rate (RNR)</b>', 'average GST rate giving <b>same revenue</b>', 'pre-GST incidence about <b>30%</b> (12% excise, 14% VAT, others)', 'at 30%, ₹10 tax = only <b>₹33</b> of ₹100 output taxed (one-third of GDP)', 'if GST taxes <b>double</b> value (two-thirds), <b>15%</b> rate still gives ₹10 = RNR', w=18),
  bx('gr', '<b>Anti-profiteering:</b> keeping a tax cut as extra profit is <b>illegal</b>. Institutions: <b>National Anti-Profiteering Authority</b>, Standing Committee, State-level Screening Committees.'),
